+# Full-Text Search Feature — Contract
+
+## 1. Search Endpoint: `GET /notes/search?q=<query>&page=N`
+
+### Behaviors
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification | Expected Result |
+|---|----------|-------------|-----------------|
+| 1.1 | Returns matching notes for keyword query | `GET /notes/search?q=python` | 200, `results` array non-empty |
+| 1.2 | Results include `snippet` field | `GET /notes/search?q=python` | Every result has `snippet` (string) |
+| 1.3 | Snippet contains `<mark>` tags around matched terms | `GET /notes/search?q=python` | First result's snippet contains `<mark>` and `</mark>` |
+| 1.4 | Results ranked by BM25 relevance (ascending rank) | `GET /notes/search?q=programming` (multiple results) | `rank` values ascend: each `>=` previous |
+| 1.5 | Phrase queries with double quotes match exact phrases | `GET /notes/search?q="chocolate chip"` | Results include Chocolate Chip Cookies note |
+| 1.6 | Results contain `id` (number), `title` (string), `snippet` (string), `rank` (number) | `GET /notes/search?q=guitar` | All four fields present with correct types |
+| 1.7 | Empty results for non-matching query | `GET /notes/search?q=xyznonexistentterm` | 200, `results` is empty array `[]` |
+| 1.8 | Returns 400 when `q` is missing | `GET /notes/search` | 400 status |
+| 1.9 | Returns 400 when `q` is empty string | `GET /notes/search?q=` | 400 status |
